externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV8NoteheadV5smuflAA17MXLSmuflGlyphNameVSgvp","title":"smufl"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/Notehead-swift.struct/smufl":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/notehead-swift.struct\/smufl","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The smufl attribute group is used to indicate a particular Standard Music Font Layout (SMuFL) character.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Sometimes this is a formatting choice, and sometimes this is a refinement of the semantic meaning of an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Notehead-swift.struct\/smufl","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"smufl"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL17MXLSmuflGlyphNameV","text":"MXLSmuflGlyphName"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"smufl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/Notehead-swift.struct":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Notehead","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Notehead","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/notehead-swift.struct","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNote.Notehead","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/Notehead-swift.struct","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The notehead type indicates shapes other than the open and closed ovals associated with note durations.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNote"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","role":"symbol","title":"MXLNote","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLSmuflGlyphName":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSmuflGlyphName"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLSmuflGlyphName","title":"MXLSmuflGlyphName","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLSmuflGlyphName"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The smufl-glyph-name type is used for attributes that reference a specific Standard Music Font Layout (SMuFL)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"character. The value is a SMuFL canonical glyph name, not a code point. For instance, the value for a standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"piano pedal mark would be keyboardPedalPed, not U+E650.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlsmuflglyphname"}}}